{% extends 'demos/live_demo.html.twig' %}

{% block demo_container %}

    <div class="max-w-[1140px] mx-auto mb-12">
        <twig:Browser class="shadow-blur shadow-blur--rainbow w-full">
            <twig:EmojiPagination :page="page" paginationRoute="app_demo_live_component_pagination" />
        </twig:Browser>
    </div>

    <section class="py-12" style="padding-top: 6rem;">
        <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
            <twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow filename="src/Twig/Components/EmojiPagination.php" reversed sticky>
The component uses the `ComponentWithPaginationTrait` from UX Pagination and
declares how to build its pagination. The trait provides the `page` LiveProp,
the `goToPage`, `nextPage` and `previousPage` LiveActions, and a cached
`pagination` result.

Here the `page` prop maps into the route path (`/pagination/{page}`) through
`UrlMapping(mapPath: true)`: change the page, and the URL itself changes.

The `perPage` prop is writable too: pick another page size and the whole
pagination recomputes, resetting to page 1.
            </twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow>
        </div>
    </section>

    <section class="py-12">
        <div class="max-w-[1400px] mx-auto">
            <twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow filename="templates/components/EmojiPagination.html.twig" sticky>
The template renders the current page items, then calls `ux_pagination()`.

`link_attributes` bridges every generated link to the Live action: the links
keep their real `href` (they still work without JavaScript, page number in
the path included), and `data-action="live#action:prevent"` upgrades clicks
to instant Live updates.
            </twig:Code:CodeWithExplanationRow>
        </div>
    </section>

{% endblock %}
